 sender's host-openable session id (the envelope's `from-session` attribute \u2014 e.g. a desktop `local_<uuid>` or a cloud session `session_`/`ses_` id), set by the sender's host so a receiving UI can link this message back to the sending session. Sender-asserted like `from`: a navigation target only, never authority. Absent when the sender's host provides none and on messages from older senders."),inbound_origin:o().optional().describe("@internal Server-asserted ingest path of the demoted delivery, copied at classification from the message-level `inbound_origin`."),senderTaskId:o().optional().describe("Task id of the in-process background subagent that sent this message, stamped by the harness from the sending loop (never from tool input). Absent for cross-session peers."),body:o().optional().describe("Decoded message body with the peer envelope stripped \u2014 byte-exact with what the model sees. Present only when the turn is exactly one harness-formed envelope (or an in-process agent message); render this instead of re-parsing the message text."),verifiedPeerPid:E().optional().describe("Kernel-verified pid of the process that connected to this session's cross-session messaging socket, read from the connection (SO_PEERCRED / LOCAL_PEERPID) \u2014 never from the payload. This identifies the CONNECTING process, which for relayed traffic (e.g. a daemon forwarding on another session's behalf) is the relay, not the message's author. Key sender identity on this, never on `from`: `from` is sender-authored and kept only for reply routing, so it is forgeable by any same-user process. Absent when unverifiable (Windows, non-UDS ingress) \u2014 never a wrong value. Pids are recyclable: provenance, not an authentication token."),handback:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Present, and always true, when the message is a subagent's final report to the agent that launched it, delivered through the SubagentHandback tool. Stamped by the harness, never from tool input. `body` is then the hand-back frame line with the indented report under it, and any harness note above it; `handbackReportText` and `handbackNote` carry those two parts for display. A boolean mark: not the `handback` state string of a task notification or of an Agent tool result. A hand-back is never joined, so neither this mark nor `flagged` appears beside `members`."),flagged:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Present, and always true, on a hand-back that auto mode's review blocked, or that it could not judge because a safety filter refused the review request: the report was delivered all the same, under the SECURITY WARNING that `handbackNote` carries. Never cap or fold such a message: show the note and the report in full. Absent on a hand-back that was not flagged, including one delivered under the note that the review was unavailable."),handbackNote:o().optional().describe("@internal On a hand-back: the note the harness composed above the frame line in `body`, without the indent. On a blocked report it quotes the review's reason, which can quote the report, so show it as untrusted text. Absent when there is no note."),handbackReportText:o().optional().describe("@internal On a hand-back: the subagent's report as the model reads it, under the frame line in `body`, without the indent. Draw it as a separate element from `handbackNote`: the two fields are their only boundary. Absent wherever `body` is and on a message that is not a hand-back."),members:C(u({body:o()})).optional().describe("@internal On a prompt that joins several queued messages from this sender: the joined messages in the order the model reads them, each with its own `body`. The origin's `body` is then absent. Absent on a message that was not joined and when any joined message had no `body`.")}),u({kind:T("task-notification"),subkind:F(["scheduled-trigger","peer-send-message","projects-relay","session-inbox"]).optional().describe("Present when the delivery is the fired stored prompt of a scheduled task/routine ('scheduled-trigger', stamped from server-asserted provenance, or declared by a local host for its own scheduled runs; the schedule attests storage, not authorship) or a coordinator co-member SendMessage delivery ('peer-send-message': model-authored text from another of the same user's sessions, verified by the server-stamped receiver co-membership \u2014 task-notification for prompt authority, but distinguishable so the receive-side crossSessionInbound setting can apply to it). The harness frames a scheduled-trigger delivery as the session's assigned task instead of the generic background-notification frame. Absent on webhook, PR-steward, plugin, and background-event deliveries."),fireReason:o().optional().describe("On a 'scheduled-trigger' delivery, why it fired: a short lowercase token such as 'scheduled', 'manual', 'retry', 'catch_up' or 'api'. Set by the server for cloud routines, or declared by a local host for its own scheduled runs, which is honored only in a process the host started with CLAUDE_CODE_HOST_SCHEDULED_RUN=1 (a local host's value is kept only if it is 1 to 32 lowercase letters or underscores); absent when neither sent one."),producer:T("session-task").optional().describe("@internal Present ('session-task') when the notification reports on work this session itself launched: a background agent, shell command, workflow, monitor, MCP or remote task settling, a detached tool call, or a hook rewake or worker check-in following up on such work. Absent on webhook, artifact and other externally-authored deliveries."),runId:o().optional().describe("On a background task's own notification: the run_id its task_* events carried, as of when the notification was queued. Not part of the text the model reads."),taskKind:T("mcp-task").optional().describe("@internal Present ('mcp-task') only on a notification that an MCP server's own task has ended, and not on every one. Narrower than task_type 'mcp_task', which also covers an MCP tool call moved to the background.")}),u({kind:T("coordinator")}),u({kind:T("unclassified")}).describe("Injected turn whose ingress classification found no provenance. Framed by the harness as a non-user source in both drains; never presumed human, never host-replayed."),u({kind:T("observer"),from:o(),senderTaskId:o()}).describe("Report from a background observer agent to the agent it observes. One-way by construction \u2014 the observed agent must not reply."),u({kind:T("auto-continuation")}),u({kind:T("observer-activity")}).describe("Activity digest delivered to an observer agent. The message body is the self-framing digest (envelope + postamble); observed content is data, not instructions.")]).describe("Provenance of a user-role message (peer session, team lead, channel). A host wrapping keyboard input must stamp {kind:'human'} explicitly \u2014 absent origin is treated as unattributed and fails closed at strict isHuman() trust gates.")),wy=f(()=>u({type:T("user"),message:X0(),parent_tool_use_id:o().nullable(),isSynthetic:M().optional(),tool_use_result:oe().optional().describe("Structured tool output \u2014 the tool's full Output object, not the string content sent to the model. The shape is per-tool, keyed by the matching tool_use block's name (see the *Output types in toolTypes); MCP and dynamic tools carry their own shapes, so the field stays unknown-typed. For the Agent/Task tool the completed shape is the subagent's final report without the model-directed agentId/usage trailer, plus run totals \u2014 render from it instead of parsing the tool_result text. A call that stepped aside for a message the user sent (today a WebFetch or WebSearch call) carries `{ detachedToolCall: true }` in place of its Output: the call is still running, and its result reaches the model in a later turn."),priority:F(["now","next","later"]).optional(),origin:fo().optional(),client_platform:o().optional().describe("@internal The `anthropic-client-platform` value of the client that sent this message (e.g. `ios`, `android`, `web_claude_ai`, `desktop_app`). Injected server-side by CCR ingress from the request header."),inbound_origin:o().optional().describe("@internal Server-asserted ingest path that produced this message. Not settable by clients."),server_received_wall_ms:E().optional().describe("@internal Epoch ms on the session server's clock when it received the HTTP request that delivered this message. Written by the session server; the CLI copies it to the turn's result as user_message_server_received_wall_ms."),historical:M().optional().describe("@internal Replayed history rather than a live message: the Remote Control bridge stamps it on the messages it flushes to the session server, which also stamps it on deliveries it replays."),shouldQuery:M().optional().describe("When false, the message is appended to the transcript without triggering an assistant turn. It will be merged into the next user message that does query."),timestamp:o().optional().describe("ISO timestamp when the message was created on the originating process. Older emitters omit it; consumers should fall back to receive time."),is_meta:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal True when the message was synthesized by the loop (not user keyboard input). From internal UserMessage.isMeta."),seeded_summon:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Desktop host only: the host's own seeded summon."),client_composed:T(!0).optional().describe("The client composed this turn from content the user did not type; the CLI delivers its text as written, with no `@path` file-mention expansion and no slash-command dispatch. On current CLIs the turn-start attachment pass is skipped as a whole: `@server:resource` MCP mentions are not expanded either, and the prompt is sent without the context the CLI normally attaches alongside it (nested `CLAUDE.md` and rules files, skill and tool listings, reminders); the pass the CLI runs between tool calls is unaffected."),text_not_typed:ka(to,T(!0).optional()).describe("@internal No person typed this message's text in this session (a server or an app composed it). The text is delivered as written and is not treated as typing: no slash-command dispatch, no at-mention expansion beyond the message's own uploaded files, no reminder or command from keywords in it, and a skill named in it does not count as typed by the user. Who sent the message, and whether a person is present, stays with its origin. The checks of whether a message's words are the user's own do not read this mark yet: they too go by the origin. Unlike client_composed, the turn-start attachment pass still runs. Any value other than false or null is read as true."),initiator:o().optional().describe("@internal The host's own label for what started this turn (e.g. the desktop app's `scheduled-task`, `sleep-auto-resume`); `user` or absent means a person sent it. Usage attribution only; it does not change how the turn runs."),is_visible_in_transcript_only:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal True when the message is stored in the transcript but not rendered in the live UI."),is_virtual:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal Display-only: rendered in the UI but filtered before API send."),is_compact_summary:T(!0).optional().describe("@internal True when this user message is a compact-summary synthetic message."),summarize_metadata:u({messages_summarized:E().int(),user_context:o().optional(),direction:F(["from","up_to"]).optional()}).optional().describe('@internal Metadata for "Summarize from here" / "Summarize up to here" summaries (from internal UserMessage.summarizeMetadata).'),mcp_meta:u({_meta:fe(o(),oe()).optional(),structured_content:fe(o(),oe()).optional(),resource_links:C(Ty()).optional().describe("CLI-owned: the `resource_link` content blocks the MCP tool returned, collected from the raw result before the CLI rewrites each into the `[Resource link: NAME] URI` text line the model reads \u2014 so a host renders the files without parsing that line. At most 50 links and 64 KiB serialized; absent when the result had none, and absent on a subagent's tool results (parent_tool_use_id set), whose mcpMeta carries `_meta` only. On today's wire this rides the mcpMeta spread as `tool_use_result.resourceLinks`. A sibling of `_meta`, never inside it: a server cannot supply it, and server `_meta` keys under the CLI-reserved `com.anthropic/` prefix are dropped before this message.")}).optional().describe("@internal MCP protocol metadata passed through to SDK consumers, never sent to the model (from internal UserMessage.mcpMeta)."),tool_result_meta:C(u({id:o(),non_execution_kind:F(Bjt).optional(),user_feedback:o().optional(),remedy:tF().optional(),permission_decision:u({decision:F(ay),source:o(),reason_type:F(Iwt).optional().catch(void 0)}).optional().catch(void 0)})).optional().describe("@internal Display metadata for this message's tool_result blocks, keyed by tool_use_id. non_execution_kind is the harness-stamped reason an is_error:true result did not carry the tool's own execution output (user-rejected / permission-rule / automode-* / interrupted / cancelled); absent means the tool ran to completion. remedy is the fix a host can offer for what the result reports (see SDKToolResultRemedy). An entry may carry a remedy alone, on a result that did run (a staged write, a sandbox violation on exit 0), so whether a call ran is read from non_execution_kind, never from an entry's presence. On a subagent's messages (parent_tool_use_id set), entries carry only permission_decision, so those messages do not say whether a call ran. permission_decision is how the call's permission check ended, as Claude Code's claude_code.tool.blocked_on_user trace span reports it. decision is accept, reject or cancelled. source names what decided: config, classifier, hook, user_temporary, user_permanent, user_reject, user_abort, or invalid_input, permission_updated_input_invalid or server_fallback_tombstone when bad input or the server ended the wait. Which label a rule gets depends on the session: in SDK sessions a rule for this session or in the user's own settings reports user_temporary, user_permanent or user_reject and other rules report config, while interactive sessions report every rule as config. reason_type is the kind of reason the check gave when it decided by itself, such as 'rule' whenever a rule decided, or 'classifier' for an auto-mode allow, which reports source config. reason_type is absent when a person or the SDK host answered the question, when the check's outcome was still a question, and for user_abort and the last three sources above. permission_decision is absent when the call ended before its permission check, and on some results built apart from the call's own run, such as a plugin hook's refusal, a hook's rewrite of a denied result, or the result the tool executor writes for a queued call that a stop cancelled. user_feedback is the deny comment a human typed at a permission prompt (the local dialog or a bridge client's deny UI), before the CLI's reject-message framing \u2014 absent when the deny was resolved by a coordinator, channel relay, or hook rather than a human. A deny answered through the SDK control protocol (can_use_tool / --permission-prompt-tool) currently reports as 'permission-rule' with no user_feedback, because that wire carries no human-provenance signal. Wrapper-level sibling \u2014 never inside `message.content` \u2014 so it is not replayed to the model. Clients read this instead of string-matching the result prose."),source_tool_use_id:o().optional().describe("@internal When this message was generated by a tool via newMessages, links it to that tool_use id."),source_tool_assistant_uuid:o().optional().describe("@internal For tool_result messages: UUID of the assistant message containing the matching tool_use block. Used for parentUuid assignment in transcript."),image_paste_ids:C(E().int()).optional().describe("@internal Paste IDs for images in this message, in order of appearance. REPL-local state \u2014 candidate for surface-side if daemon has no use for it."),plan_content:o().optional().describe("@internal Plan to implement (cleared-context flow). When set, the message is rendered with plan styling."),permission_mode:de().optional().describe("@internal Permission mode active when this message was sent (for rewind restoration)."),interrupted_message_id:o().optional().describe("@internal For [Request interrupted by user] markers only: the API msg_* id that Esc cancelled."),refused_message_id:o().optional().describe("@internal Only on the synthetic message that re-asks the same model after a refusal: the API msg_* id of the refused response. Absent when the CLI has no well-formed id for it.")})),pn=f(()=>wy().extend({uuid:p().optional(),pasted_content:C(Q0()).optional().describe("Content the user pasted into the prompt rather than typed: each entry a string or an array of content blocks. The CLI appends the text of each entry after the typed text, in order, and may wrap it in `<pasted_content>` tags. Blocks other than text are ignored; send images and documents in `message.content`. A list of over 1,000 entries and blocks in all is ignored."),inline_pastes:C(o()).optional().describe("Text the user pasted that is still in `message.content` where they put it: each entry one paste. The prompt is not changed by the host; the CLI may wrap each entry in `<pasted_content>` tags where it still stands in the last text block. It looks for the first 100 entries that are not blank. For a paste the host took out of `message`, use `pasted_content` instead."),session_id:o().optional(),agent_id:o().optional().describe("ID of the subagent that produced this message: the `task_id` of its task events, unchanged when the subagent is resumed. Absent on main-thread messages."),subagent_type:o().optional().describe("Subagent type that produced this message."),task_description:o().optional().describe("Description of the subagent task that produced this message."),file_attachments:C(oe()).optional().describe("@internal Files a remote client attached to this prompt (each {file_uuid, file_name, is_image?, sha256?, file_size?}; src/bridge/inboundAttachmentSchema.ts reads them). Typed like SDKUserMessageReplay.file_attachments so the two message types stay assignable.")}).describe("A user-role message. A client writes one to the CLI to submit a prompt (this starts a turn); the CLI emits them for user-role content it adds to the conversation itself, chiefly the tool_result blocks answering the assistant's tool_use blocks.")),sF=f(()=>wy().extend({uuid:p(),session_id:o(),isReplay:T(!0),file_attachments:C(oe()).optional()})),Ay=f(()=>u({type:T("bash_command"),command:o().describe("Shell command run verbatim, without the model and without permission checks. Trust model matches the local TUI `!cmd` path (no sandbox, no per-command prompt). By default it runs in a one-shot `/bin/sh -c` (or `pwsh`) beside the conversation, which never sees it; on a cloud worker with tengu_cloud_session_shell on it runs as the TUI's `!cmd` does, through the Bash tool (its working directory carries over to later commands and to the model's Bash calls), as a turn of its own, so the model sees the command and its output. The worker refuses some commands with a row saying why (for example a stale one, one over 65,536 characters, one containing control characters, or one sent to a host that does not run them) and skips a duplicate silently (cli/headlessHost/bashCommand.ts)."),cwd:o().optional().describe("Working directory for the command. Falls back to the session cwd when omitted. With tengu_cloud_session_shell on, the command runs in the session's current directory and one naming any other directory is refused."),uuid:p().optional(),session_id:o().optional()}).describe("@internal A user-initiated shell command. Input-only \u2014 sent by CCR clients that surface a dedicated terminal UI; never emitted on stdout. Acknowledged on arrival and, unless blank, too long or a duplicate, echoed at once as a `<bash-input>` replay row; then answered with exactly one more row: its output (a replay frame when run beside the conversation; a plain user message after its own turn when it joins the conversation, possibly followed by the model replying) or a `<bash-stderr>Not run: \u2026</bash-stderr>` replay row saying why it was refused or dropped. A blank or too-long command gets only its Not run row; a duplicate gets nothing. Other rows can come between the echo and that row.")),Xjr=f(()=>u({status:F(["allowed","allowed_warning","rejected"]),resetsAt:E().int().optional(),rateLimitType:F(["five_hour","seven_day","seven_day_opus","seven_day_sonnet","seven_day_overage_included","overage"]).optional(),utilization:E().optional(),unifiedWindows:u({five_hour:u({utilization:E(),resetsAt:E().int()}).optional(),seven_day:u({utilization:E(),resetsAt:E().int()}).optional(),seven_day_overage_included:u({utilization:E(),resetsAt:E().int()}).optional()}).optional().describe("@internal Per-window usage for the session (5-hour), weekly (7-day), and overage-included weekly (per-model bucket; present only for accounts whose responses carry that window) subscription rate-limit windows, as read from the anthropic-ratelimit-unified-* response headers. utilization is the fraction of the window used (usually 0-1, same scale as the top-level utilization field; values above 1 occur when usage legitimately runs past a window's cap, e.g. lower-priority episodes past the 5-hour limit); resetsAt is unix epoch seconds. Unlike the top-level status/utilization fields, which describe the currently limiting window, both windows are tracked on every observation, and events are emitted when a window's rounded percentage or reset time moves, not only on status transitions. Windows absent from the account state are absent here. Absent until the first response carrying these headers is observed, and always absent for API-key, Bedrock, and Vertex sessions, whose responses do not carry them."),overageStatus:F(["allowed","allowed_warning","rejected"]).optional(),overageResetsAt:E().int().optional(),overageDisabledReason:F(["overage_not_provisioned","org_level_disabled","org_level_disabled_until","out_of_credits","seat_tier_level_disabled","member_level_disabled","seat_tier_zero_credit_limit","group_zero_credit_limit","member_zero_credit_limit","org_service_level_disabled","no_limits_configured","fetch_error","unknown"]).optional(),isUsingOverage:M().optional(),overageInUse:M().optional(),overageEnabled:M().optional(),surpassedThreshold:E().optional(),rateLimitGraceActive:M().optional().describe("@internal Usage-limit grace signal. Follows the latest served main-loop or subagent response: set when it reports grace-zone utilization > 0 (the server reports that only to a request that sent `anthropic-usage-limit: extended`, tengu_lantern_spool), cleared when a response the limiter ran on reports none or, if the latest in-zone response named the grace window's reset, once that reset passes on this machine's clock. Side calls, and responses with no `anthropic-ratelimit-unified-status` (the limiter did not run), are not read. A refused request's 429 is not read either, so while requests are refused the last value persists: still expire any UI derived from this field via resetsAt. While set, overageStatus allowed / allowed_warning means paid extra usage covers the overflow (nothing will be cut off). Stays true at hard exhaustion (status rejected); combine with status instead of reading this field alone as \"still usable\"."),overagePeriodMonthly:u({utilization:E()}).optional().describe("@internal Monthly service spend-cap telemetry for the Claude-in-Slack surface (CLAUDE_IN_SLACK_V2): utilization is fraction-of-cap."),overagePeriodChannel:u({utilization:E()}).optional().describe("@internal Per-Slack-channel spend-cap telemetry for the Claude-in-Slack surface (CLAUDE_IN_SLACK_V2): utilization is fraction-of-cap. Absent when the channel has no individual cap."),limitScope:F(["service","channel","group_pool"]).optional().describe("Which spend limit blocked the request when it is not the member's own cap: 'group_pool' means a pooled group budget shared by the member's team is used up (the denial otherwise looks like the member's own monthly cap). Absent on a plain member denial and from older CLIs."),errorCode:F(["credits_required"]).optional(),canUserPurchaseCredits:M().optional(),hasChargeableSavedPaymentMethod:M().optional(),usageCreditOffer:u({kind:F(["pct_off","extra_credit"]),headlinePct:E().int(),daysLeft:E().int(),label:o()}).optional().describe("@internal A limited-time offer on usage credits the account holds at this limit, for the IDE extension's limit banner: the kind (a steeper discount, or extra credit for the same price), the headline percent every credit pack meets or beats, whole days left in the account's offer window, and the ready-made banner text. Present only on a rejected frame from a session the VS Code extension owns, once the server has answered that the account holds an active offer; absent otherwise. The prices themselves apply wherever the credits are bought.")}).describe("Rate limit information for claude.ai subscription users.")),Ge=128,nF=64,gWo=f(()=>u({session:u({total_cost_usd:E(),total_api_duration_ms:E().int(),total_duration_ms:E().int(),total_lines_added:E().int(),total_lines_removed:E().int(),model_usage:fe(o(),Bt())}).describe("Cost and usage accumulated by the current session."),rate_limits:u({limits:C(u({kind:o().max(Ge).describe("The server's meter kind, e.g. 'session', 'weekly_all' or 'weekly_scoped'. Classify a row on this, never on a label."),group:o().max(Ge).describe("The server's row group, e.g. 'session' or 'weekly'; rows render grouped under it, in the server's order."),percent:E().describe("Share of the window used, 0-100."),resets_at:o().max(Ge).nullable().describe("ISO 8601 timestamp when the window resets."),scope:u({model:u({display_name:o().max(Ge)}).nullable().optional(),surface:u({dis