).describe("@internal The browser is now in use.")),Jo=f(()=>u({subtype:T("get_sandbox_dialog")}).describe("@internal Requests the state the terminal's /sandbox dialog shows, for a host that draws the dialog with its own widgets: platform support, the policy lock, the mode and its choices, the unsandboxed-fallback override, the dependency check, the excluded commands and the configured restrictions. Read-only; a host writes through the CLI's edit-sandbox-settings subcommand.")),LW=f(()=>u({supported:M().describe("Whether sandboxing can be configured on this platform (macOS, Linux, WSL2, or Windows where enabled) and the enterprise enabledPlatforms setting includes it."),unsupported_reason:F(["wsl1","platform","excluded_platform"]).optional().describe("Why not, when supported is false: WSL1; another unsupported platform; or a platform the enabledPlatforms setting leaves out."),locked:M().describe("Whether a higher-priority settings source sets the sandbox settings, so the mode cannot be changed locally."),overrides_locked:M().describe("Whether the unsandboxed-fallback override cannot be changed from the project: set by policy (locked, or unsandboxed commands forbidden), or held closed (allowUnsandboxedCommands: false) by a --settings file or user settings."),enabled:M().describe("Whether sandboxing is running in this session: on in the settings, and the sandbox started."),enabled_in_settings:M().describe("Whether the settings files turn sandboxing on."),unavailable_reason:o().optional().describe("Why the sandbox cannot run although the settings turn it on (a missing dependency, an unsupported platform), when that is so; absent when it runs, or when it is off in the settings. When absent while enabled is false and enabled_in_settings true, the sandbox failed to start in this session."),mode:F(["auto-allow","regular","disabled"]).describe("The terminal picker's current row, from the settings: sandboxed commands auto-allowed, sandboxed with regular permissions, or no sa