or GIT_CONFIG_COUNT and its keys), which do not reach this upload\u2019s git: the grant has to stand in a file that git reads.",git_refused_not_a_repository:"Git does not recognise the .git here as a repository (\u201Cnot a git repository\u201D), so nothing was uploaded. Its HEAD, objects or refs may be missing, empty or unreadable, as after an interrupted copy. Start from a fresh clone, or from the folder that holds the real repository.",git_refused_bad_config:"Git cannot parse one of its configuration files (\u201Cbad config\u201D), so nothing was uploaded. Run `git rev-parse --git-dir` here (it changes nothing): its error names the file and the line, or the setting at fault. Fix that, then retry.",git_refused_config_unreadable:"Git cannot open one of its configuration files (\u201Cunable to access\u201D), so nothing was uploaded. Run `git rev-parse --git-dir` here (it changes nothing): its error names the file. Make that file readable for your user, or remove the include that points to it, then retry.",git_refused_unknown_extension:"This repository uses a git feature that the git on your PATH does not know (\u201Cunknown repository extension\u201D), so nothing was uploaded. Update git, or put a newer git first on the PATH that Claude Code is started with, then retry.",git_did_not_run:"The program that runs as git on your PATH started and ran no git, so nothing was uploaded. A version manager\u2019s shim (asdf\u2019s, for one) does that where no git version is set for the folder. Run `git --version` here to see what it says. Set a version, or put a real git first on the PATH that Claude Code is started with, then retry.",git_did_not_run_from_outside:"",git_dir_objects_folder_missing:"This checkout\u2019s git directory lacks objects/info or objects/pack, so nothing was uploaded. Git makes both in every repository and works without them; a copy that skips empty folders loses them. To make them again, in an ordinary checkout, at its top level, where .git is: first lo